# AUD-186 / EXT-UTILITY-LIFETIMES: docs/codebase-audit/external-exceptions.md.
# Do not suppress allocations solely by executable basename. A caller-owned leaking
# program remains a failing control even when named bash, grep, or another tool.
# EXT-CLANG-PACKAGED-DEFINEDNESS / AUD-137:
# docs/codebase-audit/external-exceptions.md. Do not restore library-wide,
# parser-wide, or instantiation-boundary masks: an undefined caller allocation
# consumed inside two libclang frames must remain observable. The external
# boundary contract checks this with the configured suppressions.

# EXT-CLANG-RECORD-FIELD-FLAG: the same verified packed-byte increment
# reaches HasFlexibleArrayMember through an instantiated record field.
# Limit this condition to the three adjacent stock-Clang instantiation frames.
# The real Sema caller-owned undefined-flag control remains an error at the
# same branch. See docs/codebase-audit/external-exceptions.md.
{
   rex_clang22_instantiated_record_field_condition
   Memcheck:Cond
   fun:_ZN5clang4Sema11ActOnFieldsEPNS_5ScopeENS_14SourceLocationEPNS_4DeclEN4llvm8ArrayRefIS5_EES3_S3_RKNS_20ParsedAttributesViewE
   fun:_ZN5clang4Sema20InstantiateClassImplENS_14SourceLocationEPNS_13CXXRecordDeclES3_RKNS_30MultiLevelTemplateArgumentListENS_26TemplateSpecializationKindEb
   fun:_ZN5clang4Sema38InstantiateClassTemplateSpecializationENS_14SourceLocationEPNS_31ClassTemplateSpecializationDeclENS_26TemplateSpecializationKindEbb
   obj:*/libclang-cpp.so.22.1
}

